+Optional prebuilt wheels that build_zip.py copies into the app's wheels\
+folder. installer\setup_runtime.ps1 installs a bundled wheel instead of
+downloading or compiling that package, so PCs without the CUDA toolkit and
+Visual Studio Build Tools also get textures and the 360 video.
+
+Make them on a PC that has the CUDA 12.4 toolkit + VS 2022 C++ Build Tools:
+    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File installer\build_wheels.ps1
+(writes nvdiffrast-*.whl and diff_gaussian_rasterization-*.whl here).
+
+*.whl files are not committed (see .gitignore). nvdiffrast and
+diff-gaussian-rasterization are licensed for non-commercial use only; a
+setup.exe that bundles them must ship their licence texts (both wheels
+contain them) and stay free / non-commercial.
