+QuokkaForm - Images To Mesh - Windows install
+=============================================
+
+QuokkaForm is free for personal, research and evaluation use. Two parts it
+uses (nvdiffrast and diff-gaussian-rasterization) are NON-COMMERCIAL only:
+see LICENSE_AND_NOTICES.txt.
+
+What you need
+-------------
+- Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit
+- NVIDIA GPU, 12 GB+ VRAM recommended (8 GB minimum), driver 551.61 or newer
+- About 15 GB free disk (packages ~8 GB + models ~4.3 GB)
+- Internet on the first run
+- Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime (already on Windows 11 and most Windows 10;
+  the installer offers it if missing)
+Not needed any more: Python, Git, CUDA toolkit, Visual Studio. (Only if the
+prebuilt texture-bake part cannot be used, see "Textures" below.)
+
+Option A - Installer (recommended)
+----------------------------------
+1. Run QuokkaForm-Setup-0.9.0.exe.
+   Windows SmartScreen may say "Windows protected your PC" because the
+   installer is not code-signed (signing costs money). Click "More info",
+   then "Run anyway".
+2. No admin rights needed. It installs for your user only to
+   %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\QuokkaForm.
+3. Accept the licence page, choose the shortcuts and whether to download
+   the models now (about 4.3 GB, recommended).
+4. The setup window then installs a private Python 3.10 and the packages
+   (10-30 minutes the first time). Then QuokkaForm opens.
+5. Start it later from Start menu > QuokkaForm (or the desktop icon).
+   It opens in its own window; no browser and no console window.
+
+Option B - Portable ZIP
+-----------------------
+1. Extract QuokkaForm-0.9.0-portable.zip anywhere (e.g. Documents).
+2. Double-click QuokkaForm.cmd. The first time it runs the same setup,
+   later it opens the app straight away.
+3. "QuokkaForm Setup.cmd" repairs or reinstalls.
+
+Repair / reinstall
+------------------
+Start menu > QuokkaForm Setup (repair), or "QuokkaForm Setup.cmd" in the
+install folder. Add -Reinstall to rebuild the Python environment:
+  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File installer\setup_runtime.ps1 -Reinstall
+
+Where things live
+-----------------
+- Program:   %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\QuokkaForm (installer) or the ZIP folder
+- Python + packages: %LOCALAPPDATA%\QuokkaForm\runtime
+- Models:    %LOCALAPPDATA%\QuokkaForm\models (models already downloaded by
+             an earlier start.bat install in %USERPROFILE%\.cache\huggingface,
+             %USERPROFILE%\.cache\torch and %USERPROFILE%\.u2net are reused,
+             not downloaded again)
+- Logs:      %LOCALAPPDATA%\QuokkaForm\logs (setup-*.log, quokkaform-*.log)
+- Settings:  %APPDATA%\QuokkaForm (settings.json, window size)
+- Outputs:   Documents\QuokkaForm\outputs\<date>_<time>_<name>\
+Uninstall (Settings > Apps, or Start menu) removes the program, Python and
+logs. It keeps your models, settings and outputs unless you tick them.
+
+Textures (diff-gaussian-rasterization)
+--------------------------------------
+Texture bake and the colour 360 video need a CUDA part that has no trusted
+prebuilt Windows download. Setup builds it automatically when the CUDA 12.x
+toolkit and Visual Studio 2022 Build Tools (C++ workload) are installed;
+otherwise it says so and everything else still works (Texture bake: None,
+video off). Install those two, then run the repair shortcut.
+
+Only one copy runs at a time: starting it again brings the open window to
+the front. It uses port 7860 on this PC only (the next free port up to 7879
+if another program has 7860).
+
+Developers (git checkout)
+-------------------------
+start.bat still works as before (needs Python 3.10, Git, CUDA 12.4 toolkit,
+VS 2022 Build Tools) and opens the browser. "start.bat --desktop" opens the
+QuokkaForm window instead. Building the ZIP and installer: see README.md,
+"Building the installer".
