+## Install (Windows app)
+
+Download **QuokkaForm-Setup-0.9.0.exe** (or the portable ZIP) and run it. No Python, Git, CUDA toolkit or admin rights needed: it installs per user to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\QuokkaForm`, sets up its own Python 3.10 and packages on first run (10-30 min) and opens QuokkaForm in its **own window** (no browser, no console). Full steps, where files live and repair: [INSTALL_WINDOWS.txt](INSTALL_WINDOWS.txt).
+
+- Windows SmartScreen may warn because the installer is not code-signed: click **More info > Run anyway**.
+- Needs an NVIDIA GPU (12 GB+ VRAM recommended, 8 GB minimum), driver 551.61+, about 15 GB free, and the Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime (on Windows 11 already; the installer offers it).
+- Data: models in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\QuokkaForm\models` (models already in the old Hugging Face / torch / `.u2net` caches are reused), logs in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\QuokkaForm\logs`, settings in `%APPDATA%\QuokkaForm`, outputs in `Documents\QuokkaForm\outputs`. Uninstalling keeps models, settings and outputs unless you tick them.
+- **Free, non-commercial**: nvdiffrast and diff-gaussian-rasterization are research / non-commercial only, see [LICENCE_FINDINGS.md](LICENCE_FINDINGS.md).
+
+## Requirements (developer setup with start.bat)
 
 - Windows 10 / 11 (primary target)
 - **Python 3.10 only** (64-bit, add to PATH during install). The prebuilt flash-attn and kaolin wheels used here are `cp310`, built for PyTorch 2.5.1 + CUDA 12.4.
 - NVIDIA GPU with CUDA (RTX 3060 12 GB tested; TRELLIS officially recommends 16 GB)
-- CUDA 12.4 toolkit and Visual Studio 2022 C++ Build Tools (needed to build nvdiffrast, diffoctreerast and diff-gaussian-rasterization on first install)
