+## Building the installer
+
+On a Windows PC with the dev setup above (its `venv` with torch is used to build one wheel):
+
+```bat
+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File installer\build_zip.ps1
+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File installer\build_zip.ps1 -Installer
+```
+
+The first makes `dist\QuokkaForm\` and `dist\QuokkaForm-<version>-portable.zip` (about 16 MB: the app, TRELLIS and FlexiCubes at pinned commits, `uv.exe`, the lock file and setup scripts; packages download on the user's PC). `-Installer` also compiles `installer\Output\QuokkaForm-Setup-<version>.exe` with [Inno Setup 6](https://jrsoftware.org/isdl.php) (or open `installer\QuokkaForm.iss` in Inno Setup and use Build > Compile after building the folder). `installer/build_zip.py` runs on Linux too. Version and publisher: `app/version.py` and the `#define`s at the top of the `.iss` (a test checks they match).
+
+- `installer\build_wheels.ps1` (optional, needs CUDA 12.4 + VS 2022 Build Tools) prebuilds nvdiffrast and diff-gaussian-rasterization into `installer\wheels\`; the next build bundles them so users never compile. Without it, setup downloads a SHA-256-pinned prebuilt nvdiffrast wheel and builds diff-gaussian-rasterization if the tools are present.
+- `python installer/build_zip.py --relock` regenerates `installer/requirements-lock-win.txt` from `installer/requirements-win.in` (needs uv).
+- The installer is not code-signed, so SmartScreen shows "More info > Run anyway".
+
